          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            The
            %em diffeomorphism group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Diff
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Diff(X)
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            of its
            = succeed "s:" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism"} diffeomorphism
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+group"} automorphism group
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            as an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SmoothMfd"} SmoothMfd
          %p
            Beware that when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is assumed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientable"} orientable
            then sometimes, but not always,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Diff
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Diff(X)
            is implicitly taken to be the group of orientation-preserving diffeomorphisms.
          %p
            In this vein if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            carries further
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extra+structure"} extra structure
            then one considers groups of diffeomorphisms which are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism"} automorphism
            preserving that extra structure. For instance
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-manifold"} G-manifold
                then one considers its
                = succeed "," do
                  %em equivariant diffeomorphism group
            %li
              %p
                if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                carries the structure of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+manifold"} Riemannian manifold
                then one considers its
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isometry+group"} isometry group
          %p etc.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#relation_to_homotopy_equivalences Relation to homotopy equivalences
          %p
            For the following kinds of manifolds
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            it is true that every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mo ≃
                  %mi Π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\alpha \colon \Pi(\Sigma) \stackrel{\simeq}{\longrightarrow} \Pi(\Sigma)
          %p
            (hence every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+infinity-groupoids"} equivalence
            of their
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+infinity-groupoids"} fundamental infinity-groupoids
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopic
            to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism"} diffeomorphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Σ
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mo ≃
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  a \colon \Sigma \stackrel{\simeq}{\longrightarrow} \Sigma
          %p
            i.e. that given
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
            there is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            with
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi Π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\alpha \simeq \Pi(a)
                  \\,.
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
                any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surface"} surface
                (
                %a{:href => "#ZieschangVogtColdeway"}> Zieschang-Vogt-Coldeway
                )
            %li
              %p
                for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Haken+3-manifold"} Haken 3-manifold
                (
                %a{:href => "#Waldhausen68"}> Waldhausen
                )
            %li
              %p
                for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
                any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyperbolic+manifold"} hyperbolic manifold
                of finite
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/volume"} volume
                and of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 3
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \geq 3
                (by
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mostow+rigidity+theorem"} Mostow rigidity theorem
          %h3#HomotopyTypeAndMappingClassGroup Homotopy type and mapping class group
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Diff
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi(Diff(\Sigma))
            of the diffeomorphism group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Diff
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Diff(\Sigma)
            is of interest (e.g.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Hatcher12"} Hatcher 12
          %p
            For instance this is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+%E2%88%9E-group"} automorphism ∞-group
            of a manifold, regarded as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/k-morphism"} k-morphism
            in an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2Cn%29-category+of+cobordisms"} (∞,n)-category of cobordisms
          %p
            Specifically, the group of connected components is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+class+group"} mapping class group
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Diff
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi MCG
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\pi_0(\Pi(Diff(\Sigma))) = MCG(\Sigma)
                  \\,.
          %h4#for_1manifolds For 1-manifolds
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Diff
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi Π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Pi(Diff(S^1))\simeq \Pi(O(2))
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Diff
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi Π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Pi(Diff(D^1))\simeq \Pi(O(1))
          %h4#HomotopyTypeForSurfaces For 2-manifolds (surfaces)
          %p
          #HomotopyTypeOfDiffClosedOrientableSurface.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+manifold"} closed
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation"} orientable
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surface"} surface
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} bare homotopy type
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ʃ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \esh(-)
              of its diffeomorphism group is
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Σ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere"} sphere
                  then
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ʃ
                                %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                                %mi Diff
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msup
                                  %mi S
                                  %mn 2
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                              %mtd
                                %mo ≃
                                %mi Π
                                %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                                %mi O
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mn 3
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mo ≃
                                %mi MCG
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msup
                                  %mi S
                                  %mn 2
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ×
                                %mi Π
                                %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                                %mi SO
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mn 3
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mo ≃
                                %msub
                                  %mi ℤ
                                  %mn 2
                                %mo ×
                                %mi Π
                                %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                                %mi SO
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mn 3
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\begin{aligned}
                        \\esh \, \big(Diff(S^2)\big) &amp; \simeq \Pi\big(O(3)\big)
                        \\\
                        \&amp; \simeq MCG(S^2) \times \Pi\big(SO(3)\big)
                        \\\
                        \&amp; \simeq \mathbb{Z}_2 \times \Pi\big(SO(3)\big)
                        \\end{aligned}
              %li
                %p
                  if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Σ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torus"} torus
                  then
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ʃ
                                %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                                %mi Diff
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msup
                                  %mi S
                                  %mn 1
                                %mo ×
                                %msup
                                  %mi S
                                  %mn 1
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                              %mtd
                                %mo ≃
                                %mi MCG
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msup
                                  %mi S
                                  %mn 1
                                %mo ×
                                %msup
                                  %mi S
                                  %mn 1
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ×
                                %mi Π
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msup
                                  %mi S
                                  %mn 1
                                %mo ×
                                %msup
                                  %mi S
                                  %mn 1
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mo ≃
                                %msub
                                  %mi GL
                                  %mn 2
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi ℤ
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ×
                                %mi B
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi ℤ
                                %mo ×
                                %mi ℤ
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\begin{aligned}
                        \\esh \, \big(Diff(S^1 \times S^1)\big)
                        \&amp; \simeq
                        MCG(S^1 \times S^1)\times \Pi(S^1 \times S^1 )
                        \\\
                        \&amp; \simeq
                        GL_2(\mathbb{Z})
                        \\times
                        B(\mathbb{Z} \times\mathbb{Z})
                        \\end{aligned}
              %li
                %p
                  in all other cases all higher
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
                  vanish:
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ʃ
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                        %mi Diff
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Σ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ≃
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi MCG
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Σ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\esh \, \big(Diff(\Sigma)\big)
                        \\,\simeq\,
                        MCG(\Sigma)
                        \\,.
            %p
          %p
            (Where for the present purpose we are writing
            = succeed ".)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi MCG
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                    %mi Diff
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} MCG(\Sigma) \coloneqq \pi_0 Diff(\Sigma)
          %p
            The first statement is due to
            %a{:href => "#Smale59"} Smale 1959
            (cf. also at
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere+eversion"} sphere eversion
            %a{:href => "#EarleEells67"} Earle &amp; Eells 67
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Gramain73"} Gramain 73
          %p
            Similarly for surfaces with
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary"} boundary
          %p
          #ContractibilityOfDiffeosOfCompactSurfaceWithBoundary.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surface"} surface
              with
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold+with+boundary"} boundary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+component"} connected component
              of the topological subgroup
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Diff
                        %mo ∂
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Diff^\partial
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible+topological+space"} contractible
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ʃ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Diff
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ∂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\esh \,
                    Diff_0^{\partial}(\Sigma)
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    1
                    \\,.
            %p
          (
          %a{:href => "#EarleSchatz70"}> Earle &amp; Schatz 1970, Thm 1D p 170
          )
          %p
            The case of surfaces with punctures is handled by
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Yagasaki01"} Yagasaki 2001
          %p
            %br/
          %h4#for_3manifolds For 3-manifolds
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ʃ
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi Diff
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Π
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ʃ
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi SO
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\esh\big(
                    Diff(S^1 \times S^2)
                    \\big)
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    \\Pi\big(
                    O(2) \times O(3)
                    \\big)
                    \\times
                    \\esh \Omega SO(3)
                    \\,.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Hatcher81"}> Hatcher 81
            )
          %p
          #SmaleConjecture.num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              %strong (Smale conjecture)
              %br/
              The bare
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism+group"} diffeomorphism group
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3-sphere"} 3-sphere
              is that of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+group"} orthogonal group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 4
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(4)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ʃ
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi Diff
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ʃ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 4
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\esh\big(
                    Diff(S^3)
                    \\big)
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    \\esh
                    \\,
                    O(4))
                    \\,,
            %p the equivalence being exhibited by the canonical inclusion
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 4
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Diff
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    O(4) \hookrightarrow Diff(S^3)
                    \\,.
            %p Also
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ʃ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi Diff
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi D
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ʃ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\esh
                    \\,
                    Diff(D^3)
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    \\esh
                    \\,
                    O(3)
                    \\,.
            %p
          %p
            After being conjectured by Smale, this was proven in (
            %a{:href => "#Hatcher"}> Hatcher 1983
            ).
          %p Generally:
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              For every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3-manifold"} 3-manifold
              the canonical map
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Diff
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Homeo
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Pi(Diff(X)) \to \Pi(Homeo(X))
            %p
              sending
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphisms"} diffeomorphisms
              to their underlying
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphisms"} homeomorphisms
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak homotopy equivalence
          %p
            That this follows from the Smale cojecture, theorem
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SmaleConjecture"}
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Cerf"} Cerf
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Hatcher78"} Hatcher, 1978
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              If a 3-manifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is not a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Seifert+3-manifold"} Seifert 3-manifold
              via an
              = succeed "-action" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Diff
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi MCG
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Pi(Diff(X)) \simeq MCG(X)
                    \\,.
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is Seifert via an
            = succeed "-action," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Diff
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Diff(X)
            are typically
            = succeed "-s." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi(S^1)
          %h2#related_entries Related entries
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism"} diffeomorphism
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+covariance"} general covariance
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isometry+group"} isometry group
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p Textbook accounts:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Augustin+Banyaga"}> Augustin Banyaga
              \:
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Structure of Classical Diffeomorphism Groups
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 400
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4757-6800-8"} doi:10.1007/978-1-4757-6800-8
          %p Further survey:
          %ul
            %li#Hatcher12
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alan+Hatcher"}> Alan Hatcher
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em A 50-Year View of Diffeomorphism Groups
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.cornell.edu/~hatcher/Papers/Diff%28M%292012.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/HatcherDiffeomorphismReview.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Discussion in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foliations"} foliations
            (and proof that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+component"} connected component
            of the diffeomorphism group of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+manifold"} closed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            is
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simple+group"} simple
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Thurston"}> William Thurston
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Foliations and Groups of Diffeomorphisms
                %strong 80
                2 (1974) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://scispace.com/pdf/foliations-and-groups-of-diffeomorphisms-8ti01j3mau.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Thurston-FoliationsAndDiffeos.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sam+Nariman"}> Sam Nariman
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Foliations and diffeomorphism groups
                %strong 71
                11 (2024) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2401.04047"}> arXiv:2401.04047
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1090/noti3080"} doi:10.1090/noti3080
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.ams.org/notices/202411/rnoti-p1471.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            The original observation that infinite-dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+groups"} smooth groups
            such as diffeomorphism groups (and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantomorphism+groups"} quantomorphism groups
            etc.) are naturally regarded as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+groups"} internal groups
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+spaces"} diffeological spaces
            –
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+groups"} diffeological groups
          %ul
            %li#Souriau79
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Marie+Souriau"}> Jean-Marie Souriau
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Groupes différentiels
              %em Differential Geometrical Methods in Mathematical Physics
              (Proc. Conf., Aix-en-Provence/Salamanca, 1979), Lecture Notes in Math.
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 836
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=607688"} MathScinet
          %h3#for_2manifolds_surfaces_2 For 2-manifolds (surfaces)
          %p
            On the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
            of the diffeomorphism group of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surfaces"} surfaces
          %ul
            %li#Smale59
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stephen+Smale"}> Stephen Smale
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Diffeomorphisms of the 2-sphere
                %strong 10
                (1959) 621–626 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1090/S0002-9939-1959-0112149-8"}> doi:10.1090/S0002-9939-1959-0112149-8
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.2307/2033664"} doi:10.2307/2033664
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/2033664"} jstor:2033664
            %li#EarleEells67
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clifford+J.+Earle"}> Clifford J. Earle
                ,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Eells"} James Eells
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The diffeomorphism group of a compact Riemann surface
                %strong 73
                4 (1967) 557-559 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/journals/bulletin-of-the-american-mathematical-society-new-series/volume-73/issue-4/The-diffeomorphism-group-of-a-compact-Riemann-surface/bams/1183528956.full"}> euclid:bams/1183528956
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#EarleEells69
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clifford+J.+Earle"}> Clifford J. Earle
                ,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Eells"} James Eells
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A fibre bundle description of Teichmüller theory
                %strong 3
                1-2 (1969) 19-43 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/journals/journal-of-differential-geometry/volume-3/issue-1-2/A-fibre-bundle-description-of-Teichm%c3%bcller-theory/10.4310/jdg/1214428816.full"}> doi:10.4310/jdg/1214428816
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#EarleSchatz70
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clifford+J.+Earle"}> Clifford J. Earle
                , A. Schatz:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Teichmüller theory for surfaces with boundary
                %strong 4
                2 (1970) 169-185 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/journals/journal-of-differential-geometry/volume-4/issue-2/Teichm%C3%BCller-theory-for-surfaces-with-boundary/10.4310/jdg/1214429381.full"}> doi:10.4310/jdg/1214429381
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#Gramain73
              %p
                André Gramain:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Le type d’homotopie du groupe des difféomorphismes d’une surface compacte
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.24033/asens.1242"} doi:10.24033/asens.1242
            %li#Yagasaki01
              %p
                Tatsuhiko Yagasaki:
                %em Homotopy types of Diffeomorphism groups of noncompact 2-manifolds
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0109183"}> arXiv:math/0109183
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.kurims.kyoto-u.ac.jp/~kyodo/kokyuroku/contents/pdf/1248-7.pdf"} pdf
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (cf.
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "#Yagasaki00"} Yagasaki 2000
          %p see also:
          %ul
            %li#Hamstrom66
              %p
                Mary-Elizabeth Hamstrom:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Homotopy groups of the space of homeomorphisms on a 2-manifold
                %strong 10
                4 (1966) 563-573 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/journals/illinois-journal-of-mathematics/volume-10/issue-4/Homotopy-groups-of-the-space-of-homeomorphisms-on-a-2/10.1215/ijm/1256054895.full"}> doi:10.1215/ijm/1256054895
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#Yagasaki00
              %p
                Tatsuhiko Yagasaki:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Homotopy types of homeomorphism groups of noncompact 2-manifolds
                %strong 108
                2 (2000) 123-136 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0010223"}> arXiv:math/0010223
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S0166-8641(99)00130-3"} doi:10.1016/S0166-8641(99)00130-3
            %li#FarbMargalit12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Benson+Farb"}> Benson Farb
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dan+Margalit"} Dan Margalit
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A primer on mapping class groups
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://press.princeton.edu/books/hardcover/9780691147949/a-primer-on-mapping-class-groups"} ISBN:9780691147949
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/j.ctt7rkjw"} jstor:j.ctt7rkjw
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://euclid.nmu.edu/~joshthom/Teaching/MA589/farbmarg.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            For the group of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+components"} connected components
            see also at
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+class+group"} mapping class group
            %em orbifold
            surfaces.
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li#ZieschangVogtColdeway
              %p
                Zieschang, Vogt, Coldeway:
                %em Surfaces and planar discontinuous groups
            %li
              %p
                J. S. Dowker,
                %em Note on the structure constants for the diffeomorphisms of the two-sphere
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2301.09487"}> arXiv:2301.09487
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %h3#for_3manifolds_2 For 3-manifolds
          %ul
            %li#Cerf
              %p
                J. Cerf,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Sur les difféomorphismes de la sphère de dimension trois (
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi Γ
                            %mn 4
                          %mo =
                          %mn 0
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma_4 = 0
                    )
            %li#Hatcher78
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Allen+Hatcher"}> Allen Hatcher
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Linearization in 3-dimensional topology
            %li#Hatcher81
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Allen+Hatcher"}> Allen Hatcher
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    On the diffeomorphism group of
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ×
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 2
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1\times S^2
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.cornell.edu/~hatcher/Papers/newDiffS1xS2.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Hatcher
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Allen+Hatcher"}> Allen Hatcher
                ,
                %em
                  A proof of the Smale conjecture,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Diff
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 3
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ≃
                          %mi O
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 4
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Diff(S^3) \simeq O(4)
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "http://www.jstor.org/pss/2007035"} jstor
            %li#Waldhausen68
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Friedhelm+Waldhausen"}> Friedhelm Waldhausen
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On Irreducible 3-Manifolds Which are Sufficiently Large
              %p
                Second Series, Vol. 87, No. 1 (Jan., 1968), pp. 56-88 (
                %a{:href => "http://www.jstor.org/stable/1970594"}> JSTOR
                )
          %h3#for_4manifolds For 4-manifolds
          %p For 4-manifolds the analogue of the Smale conjecture fails:
          %ul
            %li#Watanabe18
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tadayuki+Watanabe"}> Tadayuki Watanabe
                ,
                %em
                  Some exotic nontrivial elements of the rational homotopy groups of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Diff
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 4
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Diff(S^4)
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1812.02448"}> arXiv:1812.02448
                )
            %li#Watanabe21
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tadayuki+Watanabe"}> Tadayuki Watanabe
                ,
                %em
                  Addendum to: Some exotic nontrivial elements of the rational homotopy groups of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Diff
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 4
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Diff(S^4)
                  (homological interpretation)
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2109.01609"}> arXiv:2109.01609
                )
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (via
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graph+complexes"} graph complexes
          %h3#EquivariantDiffeomorphisms Equivariant diffeomorphisms
          %p
            On the further generality of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+map"} equivariant
            diffeomorphisms between
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-manifolds"} G-manifolds
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Augustin+Banyaga"}> Augustin Banyaga
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On the structure of the group of equivariant diffeomorphisms
                %strong 16
                3 (1977) 279-283 [
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0040-9383(77)90009-X"}> doi:10.1016/0040-9383(77)90009-X
                ]
            %li
              %p
                Kōjun Abe, Kazuhiko Fukui:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On the structure of the group of equivariant diffeomorphisms of G-manifolds with codimension one orbit
                %strong 40
                6 (2001) 1325-1337 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S0040-9383(00)00014-8"}> doi:10.1016/S0040-9383(00)00014-8
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                Kojun Abe, Kazuhiko Fukui:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The first homology of the group of equivariant diffeomorphisms and its application
                = succeed "2" do
                  %strong 1
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0703320"} arXiv:math/0703320
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1112/jtopol/jtn008"} doi:10.1112/jtopol/jtn008
